<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>Harness.Gate</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>harness-gate</AssemblyName>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    *** A C# METHOD IS NOT A CHECK AN AUTHOR CAN RUN. ***

    `Admissibility.Check` existed and was correct, and no submission could be certified admissible from
    a command line, because reaching it meant writing a program. The 5.1 skill's own Step 0 says so:
    "confirm there is a command you can actually run. If the only way to reach it is to write a
    program, the gate is NOT CHECKED." This is that command.

    It READS ONLY. It opens no socket, contacts no Portal and writes no file - the gate is a judgement
    over a submission document, and giving it any authority over the device would be a different tool.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="System.Text.Json" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Harness.Results\Harness.Results.csproj" />

    <!--
      Harness.S7, for ONE reason: gate 11's set-difference has to be computed FROM THE TAG MAP, not
      declared. A reachable set the submission stated would be the author vouching for the artifact the
      gate exists to check them against. `S7TagMap.Load` is the same reader the transport uses, so the
      gate reads the map the way the thing it is fencing reads it.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Harness.S7\Harness.S7.csproj" />

    <!--
      Harness.Device, for ONE reason and ONE type: `ProbeReport.FromStdout`, which recovers a download's
      LOAD MANIFEST from what `download-probe` emitted. The `deployment` field's arm in `Recompute`
      rebuilds the submission's object manifest from that, so the manifest is COMPARED rather than
      believed - and gate 5b's verdict is only worth reading once it is.

      *** "IT READS ONLY" ABOVE IS UNCHANGED, AND THIS REFERENCE DOES NOT WEAKEN IT. *** Harness.Device
      is the assembly that puts objects on controllers, but it does so by shelling out from methods this
      gate never calls. `ProbeReport.FromStdout` is a pure string -> record parse: no socket, no Portal,
      no process. What the reference costs is build-graph weight (Harness.Loop and Harness.Wire arrive
      behind it) and nothing else.

      *** THE ALTERNATIVE WAS CONSIDERED AND REJECTED FOR A NAMED REASON. *** Referencing only
      Ladder.Download (netstandard2.0, references nothing) would have got the probe-LOG parser and left
      the probe's json-mode `loadManifest` - the FIRST-HAND manifest, read off the live Openness
      DownloadResult - needing a second reader written here. That reader carries doctrine that is easy to
      get wrong and expensive when it is: `available: false` means NOBODY LOOKED and must never read as
      "TIA loaded nothing". A second copy of it is a second opinion that can drift from the one the
      probe's own tests pin, which is the failure this project keeps paying for.
    -->
    <ProjectReference Include="..\Harness.Device\Harness.Device.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
